er per operation)."] [224 1 "// pushFrame is step's signal that the instruction called a Python function: not an exception."] [227 1 "// callStack is call [N KWNAMES]: the callable under its N arguments on f's stack (the last len(kwnames) of them"] [228 1 "// keywords), all popped; a Python function's frame (a bound method's, its self first) made from the arguments"] [229 1 "// where they are on the stack and returned as the thread's *pushFrame, a generator made, or any other callable"] [230 1 "// called and its value pushed (202b: the arguments were copied off the stack, then again with self in front)."] [232 22 "// sys.monitoring's CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [244 24 "// the callable's slot holds self: the arguments are self's and the stack's"] [256 4 "// a built-in method bound to its object (BuiltinType's call slot): its arguments made at once with self"] [257 4 "// first (queue 210: they were copied off the stack, then again behind self)"] [286 3 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [293 1 "// directMax bounds the direct calls (callDirect) nested on the thread's Go stack at once: each holds its caller's Go"] [294 1 "// frames while its callee runs, so a deeper chain (a recursion past it, up to any recursion limit) goes on as pushed"] [295 1 "// frames, in the innermost loop, with no Go frames per Python call (queue 216d)."] [298 1 "// enter is a call's callee frame (made, its arguments bound) run from f: when f and the callee are both compiled,"] [299 1 "// directly by f's own Go code (callDirect: its value pushed on f's stack, or its exception returned); else returned"] [300 1 "// as the thread's *pushFrame, read by runFrames before the thread's next call."] [309 1 "// callDirect runs callee, a compiled function's frame called by f's compiled code (queue 216d, the user's (a) on"] [310 1 "// 216's DECISION 1): a loop of its own (runFrames, direct) with callee its entry frame, entered as runFrames enters a"] [311 1 "// pushed frame (f_back f, the recursion limit's check raising in f, the eval breaker's error in callee, no C level),"] [312 1 "// so its exception unwinds through callee's handlers and leaves it with callee's traceback entry, then f's code"] [313 1 "// returns it and f's loop adds f's; its value pushed on f's stack, or callInit's instance (an __init__ returning"] [314 1 "// anything but None the TypeError raised in f), as runFrames pushes a returning pushed frame's."] [324 1 "// runDirect is callDirect's run of callee from the running frame's compiled code: its value (callInit's instance for"] [325 1 "// an __init__), or its exception, returned to that code."] [344 1 "// callInit is the call of a class whose __init__ runs in the caller's loop (initInline; queue 210, CPython 3.14's"] [345 1 "// CALL_ALLOC_AND_ENTER_INIT): the instance made by the type's __new__ (object's) from the arguments where they are"] [346 1 "// on f's stack (k the first's position), then __init__'s frame with the instance as self in the class's slot,"] [347 1 "// returned as the thread's *pushFrame; runFrames pushes the instance when that frame returns None (TypeType's call"] [348 1 "// slot's check otherwise, raised at the call)."] [366 1 "// initInline is the __init__ a call of t (its metatype type) runs in the caller's loop (callInit): the Python"] [367 1 "// function __init__ resolves to, when t and every class of its MRO but object are class statements' (no built-in"] [368 1 "// layout), __new__ resolves to object's and __init__ is not a generator's or a coroutine's; nil otherwise, and the"] [369 1 "// call goes through TypeType's call slot. Kept on t while typeEpoch has not moved."] [397 1 "// kwnamesAt is a call's keyword names, the tuple constant i of str (-1: none), made once."] [419 1 "// step runs f's instructions until it returns (the value, nil), raises (nil, error), or calls a"] [420 1 "// Python function (nil, *pushFrame)."] [424 3 "// compiled ahead (PY8